                        // For simplicity, consume next even if it looks like option (as original does for most)
                        // But need to handle missing when next is option? We'll consume unconditionally to match --fields --join case.
                        // However for --trim etc., original reports missing when next is option. Our simple will consume and then fail parse, mismatch.
                        // To better match, we could check: if val starts with '-' and is a known option, then report missing for current?
